  "poe": {
    "budgetW": 300,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf",
    "note": "300 W across 24 PoE+ ports, i.e. 12.5 W per port on average. The port ceilings sum to 720 W, so a full 24-port 802.3at load cannot be powered: the budget covers 40 percent of the port maxima."
  },
  "notes": "M4250 series common platform: 16K MAC addresses, 4K ARP/NDP entries, 4K VLANs, static routes (894 IPv4 / 126 IPv6) plus RIP (32 IPv4), DHCP server (2K leases), sFlow, SNMP, console/telnet/SSH CLI and the AV web GUI. Rewritten from a two-line record that carried the 300 W budget but no per-port PoE, no fabric figure and no source. Quad-core 1.8 GHz ARMv8 CPU with 2 GB RAM per the datasheet specification table. Its 802.3bt sibling M4250-26G4F-PoE++ has an identical port census and a 1,440 W budget with both power supplies fitted. Sources: datasheet https://www.downloads.netgear.com/files/GDC/M4250/M4250_Datasheet.pdf and https://kb.netgear.com/000064904/NETGEAR-AV-Line-of-Fully-Managed-Switches-M4250-Series."
